    "h1": "DSCSA-Ready Blockchain Serialization for Pharma",
    "bodyHtml": "<p>The U.S. Drug Supply Chain Security Act (DSCSA) requires interoperable, electronic, unit-level tracing of prescription drugs across the supply chain. AuthiChain gives pharma manufacturers and distributors a verification layer that records each check on an immutable ledger.</p><h2>How it works</h2><ul><li>Every product scan is validated by a 5-agent AI consensus before it is recorded.</li><li>Verification results are anchored to Bitcoin L1, so the trace record cannot be altered after the fact.</li><li>Credentials follow the W3C Verifiable Credentials standard for interoperability.</li><li>A QR scan returns an authenticity result in under two seconds.</li></ul><h2>Built for regulated pharma</h2><p>AuthiChain serves pharma alongside luxury, electronics, agriculture and other regulated verticals, with plans from $49/mo.</p>",
