    "slug": "what-is-a-digital-product-passport",
    "keyword": "what is a digital product passport",
    "brand": "AuthiChain",
    "domain": "authichain.com",
    "title": "What Is a Digital Product Passport? | AuthiChain",
    "metaDescription": "A digital product passport is a machine-readable record of a product’s identity, origin and compliance. Learn how the EU DPP works and how to comply.",
    "h1": "What Is a Digital Product Passport (DPP)?",
    "bodyHtml": "<p>A Digital Product Passport (DPP) is a structured, machine-readable record of a product’s identity, materials, origin and compliance data, accessible from a scan. Under the EU’s Ecodesign for Sustainable Products Regulation (ESPR), DPPs are being introduced by product category.</p><h2>What a DPP contains</h2><ul><li>A unique product identity linked to a data carrier such as a QR code.</li><li>Origin, materials and compliance information.</li><li>A verifiable, tamper-evident record of authenticity.</li></ul><h2>How AuthiChain delivers it</h2><p>AuthiChain issues DPP-ready records as W3C Verifiable Credentials, anchored to Bitcoin L1 and verifiable in under two seconds. Plans start at $49/mo.</p>",
    "jsonLd": {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Article",
      "name": "What Is a Digital Product Passport?",
      "description": "An explainer on the EU Digital Product Passport and how to make products compliant.",
      "url": "https://authichain.com/what-is-a-digital-product-passport"
    }
  },
