    "slug": "gs1-digital-link-sunrise-2027",
    "keyword": "gs1 digital link sunrise 2027",
    "brand": "QRON",
    "domain": "qron.space",
    "title": "GS1 Digital Link Sunrise 2027 | QRON",
    "metaDescription": "GS1 Sunrise 2027 moves point-of-sale scanning to QR codes carrying GS1 Digital Link URIs — the same identifier format QRON uses to attach a signed.",
    "h1": "GS1 Digital Link Sunrise 2027",
    "bodyHtml": "<p>GS1 Sunrise 2027 moves point-of-sale scanning to QR codes carrying GS1 Digital Link URIs — the same identifier format QRON uses to attach a signed, verifiable record to every code it issues.</p><h2>Why QRON</h2><ul><li>GS1 Digital Link is the item-identity format in the AuthiChain protocol spec, not a proprietary URL scheme</li><li>One QR code serves both GS1 Digital Link resolution and Ed25519-signed verification — no second code needed</li><li>Existing GTINs and serials map directly into a verifiable record; nothing about your GS1 numbering changes</li></ul><h2>How it works</h2><p>Issue a unique identifier per unit, anchor its record on-chain for tamper-evidence, and let anyone verify it with a single scan. Plans start at $29/mo.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Does Sunrise 2027 require blockchain?</h3><p>No — Sunrise 2027 is a GS1 retail-scanning standard. Anchoring the record on-chain is optional and adds tamper-evidence on top of a compliant Digital Link QR code.</p><h3>Will our current barcodes stop working?</h3><p>No — Sunrise 2027 adds 2D scanning capability at POS; linear barcodes keep working during and after the transition.</p>",
    "jsonLd": {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@graph": [
        {
          "@type": "Service",
          "name": "QRON — GS1 Digital Link Sunrise 2027",
          "provider": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "name": "QRON",
            "url": "https://qron.space"
          },
          "description": "GS1 Sunrise 2027 moves point-of-sale scanning to QR codes carrying GS1 Digital Link URIs — the same identifier format QRON uses to attach a signed, verifiable record to every code it issues.",
